    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152">

                <pb facs="0223" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg155"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2060.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-09-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September 25,</hi> 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 13th of September, No.
                    1447, has been received, and the proceeding on your part therein mentioned is
                    approved.</p>
                <p>It is somewhat remarkable, as a coincidence, that the impression communicated to
                    you by Lord Stanley is, in sentiment and to the letter, the same which I
                    announced to Sir Frederick Bruce, at Auburn, upon reading the letter from Lord
                    Stanley, the reply to which was contained in my 2037.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
